have you ever gone to the supermarket  and realized that you spent more money  than you intended to  the primary goal of any supermarket is  that it wants its customers to spend  more time and more money without really  asking them to do so how is this  possible  well the answer lies in the structure or  the design of the supermarket store  whenever we enter any supermarket we see  trolleys kept prominently in front of  our eyes  why it's because even if the customer is  coming to purchase just one product the  trolley in her hand will make her  purchase more products just to fill up  the trolley and not be embarrassed at  the cash counter  in the initial sections we find perfumes  and beauty products for freshness which  also set the mood of the customers for  an immersive shopping experience  quite often we find the groceries  section placed at the corner or the end  of the store why is that  that's because before buying the  essential items they want the customers  to explore the store and purchase the  not so essential items  also we will never really find windows  or clocks in a supermarket to our  surprise the reason here is to make  customers escape from the real world and  not make them realize about the  excessive time that they're spending  there  and children love chocolates right which  is why chocolates are kept at the bottom  section so that children can easily grab  them and place them in the trolley  also while going to the billing counter  we find some irresistible tiny products  kept there the supermarket wants us to  top up the shopping cart with these  products even when we are paying the  bill  [Music]  have you heard of supermarkets with no  checkouts  read the first comment to know more
 

